# Cribrum

This document is the static-rendered prose half of the TEAWeb T6 demo: a
Cribrum-checked HExpr tree, parsed from Djot, elaborated to semantic
accessible HTML, then rendered. The interactive sidebar in the docs-nav
demo is a TEAWeb island that harvests its table of contents from these
very headings.

## What Cribrum is

Cribrum is a single intermediate representation — the `HExpr` — authored
as prose in Djot, elaborated into full semantic, accessible HTML,
typechecked as HTML, and checked for WCAG AA accessibility. All
conformance is expressed as nested refinements over one node type, never
a family of separate types.

## Current status

Phases 1b, 2, 3 (12 to 19 rules), 4 (16-rule conjunct), and 5 ship;
TEAWeb MVP runtime plus the typed-by-content view layer
(`TEAWeb.Html.Typed`) ship. This page is the T6 demo deliverable.

### The IR (single-tree HExpr)

One datatype, full HTML tag space, handler-capable attribute model.
`div` and `span` are two elements among many, not a catch-all.

### HTML validity as a refinement

`IsValidHtml` is a decidable predicate over `HExpr` with a total decision
procedure. A located rejection (path plus reason) is surfaced when the
decider refuses.

### AA accessibility as a refinement

Structural rules promote to type-level propositions; the non-decidable
rules stay in the checking pass forever.

## Phase order

1 then 2 then 3 then 4 then 5, with TEAWeb T0 to T4 (MVP runtime)
shipping alongside Phase 5.

### Phase 1 — Djot parser + elaborate

Phase 1a is a faithful Djot parser; 1b elaborates the surface AST into
semantic accessible HExpr.

### Phase 2 — Validity in types

The HTML content model plus per-element attribute permission as a
decidable proposition over `HExpr`.

### Phase 3 — AA checking pass

19 rules and growing; Structural / Heuristic / Runtime confidence
partition is honoured. The traversal engine walks a `(Rule, impl)`
registry rather than calling each rule by name.

### Phase 4 — Structural AA in types

16 Structural rules promoted to types. `elaborate` hard-errors on every
Phase-4 violation.

### Phase 5 — DOM render

Tiny FFI surface plus a blow-and-rebuild reconcile with focus
preservation.

## TEAWeb — Elm++ on Cribrum

The Elm Architecture realised in Idris 2, with views that are
proof-carrying HExpr. Cribrum is the substrate; TEAWeb is the first
interactive-UI consumer.

### TEAWeb runtime + dispatch

A tail-recursive interpreter loop in Idris drives the model / update /
view cycle; the only FFI boundary is Cribrum's render-to-DOM module.

### TEAWeb typed-by-content view API

Each typed smart constructor returns a child-restricted view; children
carry a compile-time witness that the catalog permits the tag.

## Convention layer

`.dj` files use class and attribute idioms that Cribrum's elaboration
understands. The convention catalog lives in `docs/conventions.md`.

## Ingest pipeline

The HTML content model and the WCAG AA rule catalog are ingested from
machine-readable upstreams (TypeScript) and compiled to Idris source.
`make ingest-check` gates drift.
